{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/814873-is-wta-to-huggy","id":814873,"title":"Is WtA to huggy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-23T09:20:33-08:00","id":814873,"title":"Is WtA to huggy?","content":"I am starting a new game and would like some pack vs pack tension. I like how territory in WtF can lead to this but is it an issue in WtA? I do not see anything really written on this in WtA, The tribes bicker over Septs and ideas but what about different packs? Most of what I see are packs having their role to play in Garou society and we all fight the Wyrm together. What am I missing? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2788-armos-black","name":"Armos Black","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T09:27:45-08:00","id":814879,"title":"","content":"Packs can compete for prestige, sept positions (for their members) and certainly the missions that present themselves. If the Wyrmfoe has leads to wyrm, who is checking it out and who is taking care of it ?<br /> Surly there is competition for that. Supernatural evil isn't that often and if a lead is promising than the garou might go great length to have their shot at Glory.<br /> <br /> Also, they might compete for cubs to join them after their Rite of Passage, or even get to mentor a cub before.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> But in general you are right. There is little evident in the books that packs go against each other for the possession of fetishes or for territories. Although each alpha might have his pack at his best, when making an approach to court the sept leaders son/daughter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T12:04:31-08:00","id":814964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/814873-is-wta-to-huggy?p=814879#post814879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in general you are right. There is little evident in the books that packs go against each other for the possession of fetishes or for territories. Although each alpha might have his pack at his best, when making an approach to court the sept leaders son/daughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>This comes down to most Septs not really having multiple packs to spare. So in bigger septs diplomatical affairs are quite a bit more noticable then in the average small sept.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T12:51:53-08:00","id":814980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/814873-is-wta-to-huggy?p=814964#post814964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This comes down to most Septs not really having multiple packs to spare. So in bigger septs diplomatical affairs are quite a bit more noticable then in the average small sept.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>pretty much this. I have had some memorable pack rivalries when a Sept has more than 1 pack of similar rank. And since you can alter numbers of Garou present for your own game, or just set it at a larger Sept, this can be very easy to accomplish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:34:12-08:00","id":815035,"title":"","content":"Privileges. You could give a number of enticements in game to the most respected and currently in favor pack. Sept positions opening up, stories told about individuals in the pack or pack deeds by npcs or higher ranking garou, opportunities to mentor or teach other Garou (someone wants to learn something, they send them to soneone they trust and favor who's in a pack), open discussions about Ranking up and preparing to be more responsible and respected in the Nation, rewards of learning rites of respect, taking roles in moots, pack being given a place sitting closer to the septs Alphas at meetings and moots. Arranging matings (giving characters dots in kinfolk if not wanting to play it out).<br /> <br /> A prized fetish, a quest to gain something for the Sept/Caern. Given a territory to defend and call home for the pack.<br /> <br /> a lot of things can be dangled for those packs that want it, and hopefully seeing them get it will push others forwards for wanting it. If not...well then the others clearly arent ready if they cant put the needs of Gaia, the Nation and the Sept as a high enough priority to act for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> hope that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:04:48-08:00","id":815061,"title":"","content":"The Pack Status rules from W20 Rage Across the World is probably a good basis for pack vs. pack politics. It sets up a social currency system where packs earn Status (mostly via pack Renown rewards), and can spend it for various things around the Sept (like claiming a Fetish). It's not designed for pack vs. pack but it shouldn't be hard to adapt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T20:52:35-08:00","id":815222,"title":"","content":"Philosophy is usually plenty of ground for conflict in WTA LARP. Heal vs. Destroy, Collaborate vs. Insulate, and of course, every Pack develops in-jokes and secret shames.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T22:27:25-08:00","id":815262,"title":"","content":"Reduce the power of external enemies (no Pentex squads or banes hunting down all werewolves), limit the amount of resources available to all Garou, bring in some ethical disagreements over tactics (two groups of vampires are fighting each other - ally formally or informally with the nicer group, or attack them both, at the risk of causing them to have to work together? A group of human nature-loving hippies are building a commune in the middle of the forest - encourage or slaughter?), and the tension should appear on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T22:34:40-08:00","id":815266,"title":"","content":"Or to put it more succinctly: the Garou nation is a natural powder keg always on the brink of exploding, artificially kept together by the enmity of the Wyrm. Rage filled Glass Walkers, Red Talons, Black Furies, Sliver Fangs, and Shadow Walkers, all working together - now that's the unnatural situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T01:26:23-08:00","id":815307,"title":"","content":"In the modern era, the Garou have their collective backs up against a wall and infighting is not so common as it once was. Historically speaking, the Garou havewarred with each other quite a bit to control land; during the Second War of Rage, the Pure tribes fought bitterly to hold their territory against the encroaching European tribes. Even the numerous 'Wyrmbringers' have spats about who will control what when the Wendigo and Uktena are driven out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T20:15:02-08:00","id":816617,"title":"","content":"It also depends on the purposes of the packs in your games. Many packs are created within a Sept for a purpose and disbanded when that purpose is fulfilled. Others are generations-old with new members coming in when old ones die, or leave for various reasons.<br /> <br /> Many Septs may simply not be big enough to support multiple packs to vie for power, but that doesn't mean that there aren't individuals in a Sept that are trying to gain control and build/recruit/manipulate packs to help prop them up and support them too.<br /> <br /> If you have a sept of 13, chances are that you may have one or two active packs, while others have joined together as a temporary pack just to give them a pack to be with until another purpose comes along.<br /> <br /> For the purposes of most games, a player-pack will join together for a purpose, and will remain together for the rest of that chronicle (because, well, you don't want to break up the party, and you don't want to inject too many NPCs into a pack either in most cases.)<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how Foresaken handles their packs, but in Apoc, tension between packs may be less about the local Sept, but maybe on a larger scale where two packs are backing different factions, competing for the same Fetish, seeking to be accepted by a certain Totem who only takes one pack at a time, or is seeking to control a territory that they feel they have the right to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T08:25:22-08:00","id":816899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/814873-is-wta-to-huggy?p=816617#post816617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also depends on the purposes of the packs in your games. Many packs are created within a Sept for a purpose and disbanded when that purpose is fulfilled. Others are generations-old with new members coming in when old ones die, or leave for various reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get packmembers dying or retiring but entering or leaving packs on a regular basis always seemed odd to me, especially with every other description of packs telling us, that the ties amongst packmates are especially strong and intimate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T20:09:10-08:00","id":817356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/814873-is-wta-to-huggy?p=816899#post816899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get packmembers dying or retiring but entering or leaving packs on a regular basis always seemed odd to me, especially with every other description of packs telling us, that the ties amongst packmates are especially strong and intimate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that the intimacy has to do with the spiritual bond created through the Rite that creates the pack. A pack is often formed for a purpose. Sometimes those purposes are short (a mission, albeit short or lengthy), or longer (a long-term goal, or as a purposeful family.) But when one's Tribe comes calling, when a Sept has to split, or when another Pack loses its Ahroun, and you have more than your fair share of them, sometimes the pack needs to break off a few, or break up when the time is right. That doesn't mean that you won't have a lingering bond (after all, you fought, bled, and sometimes died for one another), but the ritual of creating a new pack will fill in that longing and give you new commitment too.<br /> <br /> I'll try to find sources that back up my thoughts on packs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","user":"Torakhan","date":". 01-26-2016, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T20:26:31-08:00","id":817368,"title":"","content":"I think competition between packs within a sept should usually be within limits (unless the ST really wants a civil war type plot). Smaller septs should have little rivalry, but big septs with powerful caerns will have more internal politics.<br /> <br /> If the packs belong to different septs/protectorates though, then rivalry can get fierce and even descend into war. Especially in historical chronicles. Nowadays, conflicts are likely more rare unless it involves the traditional tribal rivalries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T20:28:31-08:00","id":817370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/814873-is-wta-to-huggy?p=817356#post817356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A pack is often formed for a purpose. Sometimes those purposes are short (a mission, albeit short or lengthy), or longer (a long-term goal, or as a purposeful family.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the kind of pack that exists will impact the potential for rivalry/conflict with others. Not all packs will claim territory/protectorates. However, even those packs that don't might find themselves trespassing the territory of those packs that do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T09:43:21-08:00","id":817700,"title":"","content":"&quot;<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Most of what I see are packs having their role to play in Garou society and we all fight the Wyrm together. What am I missing? Thanks.</span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">&quot;<br /> <br /> You might be missing the fact that the history of the Gaian shapechangers is full of meaningless violence, genocide and attempted genocide <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T02:28:20-08:00","id":818303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/814873-is-wta-to-huggy?p=817356#post817356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the intimacy has to do with the spiritual bond created through the Rite that creates the pack. A pack is often formed for a purpose. Sometimes those purposes are short (a mission, albeit short or lengthy), or longer (a long-term goal, or as a purposeful family.) But when one's Tribe comes calling, when a Sept has to split, or when another Pack loses its Ahroun, and you have more than your fair share of them, sometimes the pack needs to break off a few, or break up when the time is right. That doesn't mean that you won't have a lingering bond (after all, you fought, bled, and sometimes died for one another), but the ritual of creating a new pack will fill in that longing and give you new commitment too.<br /> <br /> I'll try to find sources that back up my thoughts on packs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that is not the way I see garou behave. It is to logical, to weaver, to unemotional.<br /> <br /> Albrecht's pack, as well as the silver river pack, met by chance. Sure, in case of the latter Uktena manipulated a little to bring them together and kind of made them into a pack by acting as their totem. But besides that, there is no ritualistic formation of a pack. Sure, Book of auspices gave us a rite to form packs for specific reasons, and the Rite of the Phonix before that, but my guess is most packs form due to circumstances, but stay together afterwards.<br /> They aren't military companies, where the generals assign, or re-assign people as they see fit. They are more like friends, who grew together to form a near perfect social group and that can't be forced.<br /> <br /> In any case, I dont believe that there is a rite that makes a pack from zero to hundred in a dice roll. The rite in the book of auspice is for temporary packs mainly, and I didn't read it's description as a retcon to all of 2nd Edition as in &quot;this rite is by the way the usually means of forming packs, even though we never thought about it, until revised edition&quot;.<br /> And even the Rite of Totem, that kind of was described as the formation of a pack rite, is for a group of garou who already have bonded in a way, that they want to cement by choosing the same Totem as their spiritual guide. But there are packs without Totems. And while some garou might see them as something lesser than a pack, they don't feel that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T04:41:45-08:00","id":818334,"title":"","content":"What most printed Caerns and Septs point is that it's very rare for an actual pack to have the complete control of such a place. I think that as presented all the packs and their members have a special bond. This bond is one of love and intimacy, but it's also highly colored by the fact that the Garou are highly emotional and volatile.<br /> <br /> Just look at what the life of the PC's looks like. Heck, they even lead luckier lives then the average pack will. There will be blood. There will be loss. There will be tensions. There will be extreme emotions. I think everyone here has experienced a volatile relationship with huge ups and downs. Some people can cope and keep together... others will drift away. And this is the important bit I think, a pack will break. The members will still feel hugely for each other, but they will realise that the best thing for each other is to give themselves space.<br /> <br /> I think this is what happen with the Shapeshifters as they grow older. Their myths increase at the same rate as all the losses do. They become grumpier and more ornery and they look more towards of doing things like &quot;they should be&quot; rather then what they want to do. In a way, they grow up and cope with a world where just being yourself and having the gang of best friends is just not enough. Add to that your family and the ties outside the Shifters, and you're up for a harsh life.<br /> <br /> This means that some of them will be recruited for political, religious or even martial causes. These causes and postings are so easy to pick up when you consider how much stress just hanging around and adventuring with your pack actually is. I assume this is the reason why the Caerns and Septs are led by people who are in no way connected as packs. I play this up by introducing broken packs as a matter of course, and some times even exploring what got them to that point - I've had amazing success by tying the story into the tale of how a pack grew sour and why they avoid, fight or pretend not to care about each other.<br /> <br /> This same dynamic applies as a whole to all the shifters. We usually inspect how much Rage colors their interactions with humans, but it makes their interactions among themselves even harder. Combine that with the number of political, philosophical, religious, military and cultural movements they could be members of and it's quite clear that even the general common goal and purpose of the Garou cannot really keep it all working as it should.<br /> <br /> The idea behind PC packs that actually want to fight against the Apocalypse is actually getting people to get beyond themselves and actually work together if they want. It's why Margrave Konietzko's movement exists as an attempt at a NPC group pursuing the same goal.<br /> <br /> Heck, everything considered, it's amazing it works as well as it does!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>